<title>ESTONIA: TALLINNA FARM SEES 10 PCT RUSSIA TARIFF.</title>
<headline>TALLINNA FARM SEES 10 PCT RUSSIA TARIFF.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonian drug firm Tallinna Farmaatsiatehas said on Monday it may be able to send its goods to Russia at an export tariff of 10 percent rather than 20 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;We have heard from several sources that the possibility to enter the Russian market with 10 percent tariffs is not ruled out for the summer,&quot; chairman Priit Kivi told the company's shareholder meeting.  </p>
<p>&quot;This is not big as a percentage but it is big as a sum,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Most of the company's output is exported and most of that goes to Russia.</p>
</text>
